    "asOf": "2026-10-07",
    "items": [
      {
        "text": "State Rep. Tracy Katz Muhl, an attorney, has represented the 57th District since 2024. She previously led the Northbrook School District 28 Board of Education, where she says she implemented free full-day kindergarten, and she serves as the Northfield Township Democratic committeeperson. She has volunteered with Moms Demand Action and LGBTQ+ advocacy groups.",
        "cites": [1, 2, 3],
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "State Rep. Tracy Katz Muhl, an attorney, has represented the 57th District since 2024.",
            "cites": [1]
          },
          {
            "text": "She previously led the Northbrook School District 28 Board of Education, where she says she implemented free full-day kindergarten, and she serves as the Northfield Township Democratic committeeperson.",
            "cites": [2]
          },
          {
            "text": "She has volunteered with Moms Demand Action and LGBTQ+ advocacy groups.",
            "cites": [3]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "In the legislature, she sponsored \"Karina's Law\" to remove guns from domestic abusers. She also sponsored laws regarding treated wastewater for industry use and outpatient mental health treatment. She says she has passed legislation on reproductive health care. She has proposed allowing community colleges to offer bachelor's degrees. She also sponsored bills to restrict cell phone use in schools and require cable outage credits.",
        "cites": [4, 1, 2, 5],
